00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:48.150
Let's jump into the first point.

00:03:48.150 --> 00:03:50.420
What is the GMAT, why it is so important?

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:53.330
GMAT stands for Graduate
Management Admission Test,

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:55.600
and it is an entry exam
required by pretty much

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:58.285
all prestigious graduate
level business programs.

00:03:58.285 --> 00:04:01.550
So both the pre-experience master programs

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:04.170
but also the post-experience MBA programs

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:05.210
to get admitted to them.

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:06.810
So this means that if you wanna get

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:09.380
into one of the globally
leading business programs

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:12.750
on a graduate level, you really
need to take the GMAT exam

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:14.260
and you will need a good score

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:16.960
in order to get admitted to
the absolute top programs.

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:18.220
So, what is the exam?

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:20.580
Nowadays consists of four parts.

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:22.680
First, the analytical writing assessment,

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:24.400
second, integrated reasoning,

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:27.470
third, the quant part, and
fourth, the verbal part.

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:29.350
So let's briefly go over these components.

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:30.800
Let's start with the first one,

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:32.200
the analytical writing assessment.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.390
In this section, you're
required to write a short essay

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:37.250
to a specific question that
you are given then in the exam.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:39.390
The main reason why
this exists in the exam

00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:41.610
is that the business quits wanna make sure

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:43.940
that you actually wrote your essays,

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:45.960
your application essays, yourself.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:48.940
If your application essays
are flawless English,

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:52.113
but you score really bad on
this analytical essay exercise

00:04:52.113 --> 00:04:54.380
then most likely, this
means that you actually

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:56.280
did not write your essays yourself,

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:58.230
but you probably had a ghost writer.

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:00.320
What this means for you is
that this section of the exam

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:02.400
is pretty much only a hygiene factor.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:05.090
It is not too difficult to
score on the higher segments

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:06.390
of the section of the test

00:05:06.390 --> 00:05:08.290
and if your answer's just above average,

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:10.210
this should usually be
fine for most schools,

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:12.470
here you wanna make sure
that you are not raising

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:15.350
any red flags by having a
score which is really low,

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:17.070
especially if this is not matched at all

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:19.450
by the quality of your
other application assets.

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:22.000
Integrated reasoning is the
second section of the test,

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.090
here they have different
types of exercises

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.840
where they show you charts, data, diagrams

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:28.450
and they just want to
see how when you are able

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:30.460
to draw conclusions from these things

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:31.370
that are presented to you.

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:33.920
The section was introduced
to the exam in 2012,

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:35.390
it did not exist before that

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:38.397
and it is not part of
the final GMAT score,

00:05:38.397 --> 00:05:41.380
and for these reasons, it is
not that important this way.

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:43.450
Just make sure that you
score above average,

00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:45.690
here you do not want
to raise any red flags

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:47.420
by having an especially bad score,

00:05:47.420 --> 00:05:49.370
but usually if you score
well in the quantum,

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:51.000
the verbal part, there should be no reason

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.550
why you shouldn't be able to
also score here high as well,

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:55.350
so make sure that you familiarize yourself

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:57.410
with the types of question
that you're able score

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:59.340
on a solid level, but this is not what

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:01.210
will make or break your
application in the end,

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:02.540
especially if you have at least

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:04.370
an average or above average score.

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:06.910
Now to the two really important
and interesting parts,

00:06:06.910 --> 00:06:09.150
and this is the quant
part and the verbal part.

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:10.820
As you can see also time-wise,

00:06:10.820 --> 00:06:13.480
these two parts make the
majority of the test,

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:15.710
and from the scores of these two sections,

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:18.550
your final GMAT score will be built

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:20.920
the combined score that
can come out of the verbal

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:24.190
and quant section would
range between 200 and 800,

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:25.970
so this is the range of
scores that you can get,

00:06:25.970 --> 00:06:28.400
and this is the main
score that you will use

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:30.220
for your business school applications,

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:32.670
this is really the key section
where you wanna score well,

00:06:32.670 --> 00:06:34.810
this is the section that
you wanna prepare for,

00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:36.480
this is the score that matters,

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:38.510
this is what business
schools look out for.

00:06:38.510 --> 00:06:39.600
So, what scores do you actually need

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:41.150
in order to get admitted to

00:06:41.150 --> 00:06:43.670
a top business school
graduate level program?

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:46.130
Let's look into the statistics
of some MBA programs,

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:49.100
because most people will
do the GMAT for an MBA.

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:51.880
As per the Current Financial
Times global MBA ranking,

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:54.580
the program that is at the
moment ranked number one,

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:57.140
is the Harvard Business
School MBA program.

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:59.780
If you look into the
official latest class profile

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:04.680
of the Harvard MBA, the
median GAMT score is 730.

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:08.700
So 730 out of 800, and
the total range deviates

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:12.270
between 590 and 800, this
is pretty impressive,

00:07:12.270 --> 00:07:14.810
because there are only a
couple of people worldwide

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:18.500
to actually achieve a perfect
800 score on the GMAT exam,

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:20.370
but this also shows you that you can study

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:23.360
at Harvard Business School
with a GAMT of only 590,

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:24.750
which is indeed quite a low score

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:26.540
for such a leading MBA program.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:28.320
However, what you also need to recognize

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:30.900
is that if you look
outside of the US programs,

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:32.930
the more local programs
tend to have GMAT average

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:34.420
just with just significantly lower.

00:07:34.420 --> 00:07:35.460
Just as an example,

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:37.750
let's look into the
best German MBA program,

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:41.140
it's on ranked 64 on the
Current Financial Times ranking,

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:44.970
it is the WHU MBA program,
they do not disclose

00:07:44.970 --> 00:07:47.570
the exact average in the class,
though they talk about that,

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:49.860
from their perspective most MBAs schools

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:52.890
require GMAT score above
600 to get admitted,

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:54.610
and just from a bit off desk research,

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:56.180
reading online forums and so on,

00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:58.440
I concluded that the average of the WHU

00:07:58.440 --> 00:08:00.340
is probably around 650,

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:02.030
so why this is not an efficient number,

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:04.330
you can see that it is significantly below

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:07.190
the top MBA programs,
and it is much easier

00:08:07.190 --> 00:08:10.670
to get a score of 650 than
to get a score above 700.

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:13.860
So, how difficult is it really
to score high on the GMAT?

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:16.510
What I have prepared for you
here is a percentile table

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:19.200
where you can see in
what percentile you fall

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:22.040
depending on the total
score that you achieve.

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:24.150
The percentiles change a bit year on year,

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:27.630
but the mean score is 545 on the GMAT.

00:08:27.630 --> 00:08:29.970
If you want to belong to the top 20%

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:31.930
of the GMAT test takers, you need to

00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:34.137
a score of at least 660.

00:08:34.137 --> 00:08:36.123
The score that most people try to go for,

00:08:36.123 --> 00:08:38.190
and the score that most people try

00:08:38.190 --> 00:08:41.717
to consider really competitive
for the best programs is 700,

00:08:41.717 --> 00:08:45.200
and what you can see here is
the 700 roughly corresponds

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:48.010
to the top 10% of GMAT test takers,

00:08:48.010 --> 00:08:49.610
and if you want to be part of the top 1%

00:08:49.610 --> 00:08:54.610
of GMAT test takers, you
need to score 760 or above.

00:08:54.860 --> 00:08:56.870
Of course, you need to be
aware that those people

00:08:56.870 --> 00:08:59.070
who take the GMAT usually have completed

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:01.920
at least one undergraduate
university degree,

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:04.150
they're applying for
masters, an MBA degree,

00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:06.230
which shows they have
some level of ambition,

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:08.710
so it might be more difficult
than in other groups

00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:11.570
to score within the
top 10% of test takers.

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:14.107
Let's start with some overall
GMAT test prep advice.

00:09:14.107 --> 00:09:15.980
So, what did I do to score away

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:17.460
with three weeks of preparation?

00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:19.013
The first thing that
really worked well for me

00:09:19.013 --> 00:09:22.210
is that I made sure that the
time I prepare for the GMAT

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:24.470
is really blocked by that.

00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:27.270
I didn't wanna be distracted
by any other activities,

00:09:27.270 --> 00:09:30.170
I didn't wanna go to the
university or go to a job

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:32.840
and then only in the evening
be able to work on my GMAT.

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:35.490
I blocked three weeks and
really dedicated myself

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:37.860
to GMAT preparation full time.

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:41.130
This way I put my full attention
on the GMAT preparation

00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:43.140
every single day of the three weeks,

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:44.520
and this meant that I learned usually

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.920
more than six hours each of these days.

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:49.180
Of course I could have gone
even longer, but at some point

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:52.070
your brain just isn't able to
process the material anymore,

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:53.160
at least mine isn't.

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:54.560
I had several friends at the time

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:56.134
who didn't wanna do that,
they continued to go

00:09:56.134 --> 00:09:59.530
to university or to their
job, and then only learn

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:01.970
for the GMAT maybe at the
evening or at the weekends.

00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:03.980
If you do this and are
still able to score, well,

00:10:03.980 --> 00:10:05.590
you have my highest respect,

00:10:05.590 --> 00:10:07.500
but what just I have observed from myself,

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:09.520
is just so much more difficult.

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:12.200
If after a long work, you've
work already many hours,

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:15.410
then in the evening you wanna
concentrate yourself again

00:10:15.410 --> 00:10:17.920
and try to learn, try to
get into the material,

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:19.510
this is just so challenging.

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:22.190
If you're somehow able,
really blocked yourself

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:23.620
the time for a couple of weeks

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:25.260
and then you will be much better off.

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:28.086
My second insight is, that
when you learn for the GMAT,

00:10:28.086 --> 00:10:31.970
the Pareto principle or the
80 20 rule really holds true.

00:10:31.970 --> 00:10:33.860
After a couple of weeks of preparation,

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:36.710
you very quickly reach a certain plateau,

00:10:36.710 --> 00:10:39.390
and if you reach that and then
you wanna further improve,

00:10:39.390 --> 00:10:41.300
the time that you need to improve further,

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:43.870
will just go up exponentially,
and at some point,

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:45.450
you just need to ask yourself

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:47.390
whether the time invested
is worth it or not.

00:10:47.390 --> 00:10:49.790
For me, probably that
point came after two weeks.

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:51.920
After two weeks I started to realize

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:55.430
that my progress really
slowed down significantly

00:10:55.430 --> 00:10:58.400
and my strategy was that
already had the GMAT tested

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:00.220
after week three of my preparation,

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:01.590
and if I would not have achieved

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:02.800
the test result that I wanted,

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.400
I would probably have rescheduled

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:06.380
to another test date in the future

00:11:06.380 --> 00:11:07.460
because as you might know,

00:11:07.460 --> 00:11:11.250
you're able to directly
cancel your GMAT test results

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:13.500
in a few minutes after
you complete the test.

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:15.660
The next key piece of preparation advice

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:18.780
is that you show to really do mock tests.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:20.090
And the one that I liked best,

00:11:20.090 --> 00:11:23.180
that I felt like resembled
most the extra tests in the end

00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:25.050
was the Manhattan Mock Test.

00:11:25.050 --> 00:11:27.370
You can either buy access
to it on their website

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:29.430
