00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:37.840
the Manhattan prep exam
really closely resembles

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:39.010
the real thing in the end.

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:40.380
So how exactly did I do it?

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:42.540
So after two or three days of studying,

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:44.410
so after I got the basic concept

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:47.190
of what the GMAT was all
about, I decided to take

00:11:47.190 --> 00:11:50.320
the very first mock exam to
set a baseline for myself,

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:52.290
so to understand from where I'm starting.

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:54.297
And I remember that
these two or three days,

00:11:54.297 --> 00:11:56.270
I scored slightly above 600,

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:58.990
so it was a 610 or 620
